# Django / Python

## Layering

```text
views / API / management commands  →  request/services.py  →  models.py
```

- Put reusable business logic in `services.py`, not duplicated in views, API handlers, or CLI
- Project package: `conf/` with split settings under `conf/settings/`

## Management commands (CLI)

Human and agent use the same doors: `python manage.py <command>`.

- Naming: `<entity>_<action>` (e.g. `thing_list`, `thing_show`)
- List/show commands: support `--json` for stable stdout (agents parse JSON; humans can omit it for tables)
- Example: `.venv/bin/python manage.py thing_list --json`
- Commands call `request/services.py` only — no raw ORM in command classes
- Register each agent-facing command in `AGENTS.md` (one line: purpose + flags)

## Habits

- Migrations: one logical change per migration
- Use `.venv/bin/python` for `manage.py` and tests (or activate the venv first)
- Tests only when requested or they cover meaningful behaviour

## Imports

- Cross-app: absolute from app package (`from request.models import Thing`)
- Same app: absolute or single-dot relative (`from .models import Thing`)
- Never use multi-level relative imports across apps (`from ..otherapp import ...`)